00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:35.440
When the Wild Beast's Match was over,

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:39.090
only Mattis still stood, triumphantly becoming the new chief.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.490
Borka, who lost the match,

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:47.140
grew further depressed upon learning his son, 
Birk, didn't want to become a robber.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:52.990
But the two chiefs made up their minds to keep enjoying...

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:55.500
their joyful robber's lifestyle together eternally.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:01.590
The Shout of Spring

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:01.590
The Shout of Spring

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:28.800
I told you, old men have no business going out and freezing to the bone,

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.380
just to watch the Wild Beast's Match!

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:39.730
I might as well just lie here and stare, rather than sit up and stare.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:46.480
Then you just lie there and...

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:52.040
listen to me regale you with news of my new life as chieftain of all the robbers.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:56.820
Borka's doing well, too, he's even restraining his loud mouth, mostly.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:00.200
He's actually quite a clever, daring fellow.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.890
It's quite a joy for me to behold!

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:10.200
And now, with the two of us working together, we're bringing in one fine haul after another.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:13.900
We're handily outfoxing the sheriff's men,

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:16.160
and that's a joy for everyone to behold!

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:23.980
Soon, Mattis' forest will be completely free of all those obnoxious soldiers.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:32.140
Yeah, yeah. Brag when you're riding home.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.960
That's a bold attitude for someone so scrawny!

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:38.150
Old man!

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:41.800
Ta-da!

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:46.010
If you put this on, your chill will be banished instantly!

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.660
Oh my!

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:53.260
You look more regal than any count!

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:56.640
Wow, that's a surprise, huh?

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.650
When did you get such a nice fur—

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:04.370
Don't startle me!

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:07.520
My haul is also—

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:08.920
You guys!

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:11.340
Clean up before dinner!

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:15.480
I'll blow you right into the depths of hell!

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.080
Hey, Klippen!

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:22.360
It's got a mind of its own!

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:31.370
Don't snuggle up so tightly to me!

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:39.530
At last, this poor old man is just about to start thawing out.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:46.260
Your body is as warm as glowing embers.

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:14.060
You are not a rumphob clinging onto a bear's belly,

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:16.900
so just give me a little space...

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:33.300
Looky there!

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:42.500
Yeah, the snakes and earthworms have gone underground.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:47.270
The sketchy things in the forest have gone away somewhere, too.

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:56.120
Yeah, you never know when the empty forest will drag even you two underground.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:06:02.130
Oh, then I'll just wake up the spiders and ants sleeping down there,

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:05.890
and drag them out onto the soft, wet moss.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:08.890
We're back!

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:09.680
Ahchoo!

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:12.540
So cold...

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:14.890
The rains lately are so chilling.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:19.640
What's up? Preaching at these two?

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:20.850
Old man!

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:24.370
Snake boy and our little wild harpy.

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:28.150
Such an old man's sermon must be like preaching to the deaf.

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:35.660
That aside, if you listen to the tale of what we just did in the forest, you'll learn more.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:40.080
Even though it's the tale of some filthy scumbag robbers?

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:41.380
You!

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:47.420
Hey! Go back to your nest already, snake boy.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:53.210
Your father might be waiting for you, equally caked in filth.

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:06.690
This is the way I like it while I'm waiting.

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:10.380
What are you waiting for?

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:15.090
Well, what do you think?

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:38.930
Hey, what do you think is the matter with Skalle-Per?

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:41.510
Old age.

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:45.580
But he won't die of it, will he?

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:48.730
Yes, it happens.

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:51.350
What?!

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:55.760
I'll never stand for that!

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:58.330
Damn it to the depths of hell!

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:05.030
You decide a lot of things,

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:09.850
but you won't be deciding this,

00:08:09.850 --> 00:08:11.050
Mattis!

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:47.800
Was the baby born?

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:54.530
Mattis...

00:08:55.380 --> 00:09:00.720
It's the best name for a strong chieftain of robbers.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:15.830
Time passed, and Skalle-Per grew weaker and weaker.

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:19.980
Per.

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:27.250
These days, he just lies there with his eyes closed.

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:53.540
Joen, come!

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:14.420
H-He...

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:17.460
He's dead!

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:21.140
I most certainly am not.

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:32.100
Don't you think I'd have enough manners...

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:37.520
...to say goodbye before I went away?

00:10:52.550 --> 00:10:56.100
But... Now...

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:08.350
Now, my friends, I take my leave of you all.

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:17.320
Now I shall die...

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:37.040
He's always been here.

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:43.050
And now he's not!

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:50.540
This man!

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:53.840
Was always!

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.850
Here!

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:00.540
But!

00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:03.430
Now!

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:06.730
He isn't!

00:12:15.590 --> 00:12:18.280
This man was always by my side...

00:12:18.770 --> 00:12:23.800
But now he's not!

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:25.010
Hey, Mattis.

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:30.320
No one can always be there.

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:35.120
We are born, and we die.

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:37.420
That's how it's always been.

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:40.550
What are you complaining about?

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:46.800
But I miss him!

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:48.970
Without that man...

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:53.290
I miss him so much, it rends my heart!

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:59.600
Would you like me to hold you for a bit?

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:11.620
Yes, you might as well.

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:13.930
And Ronja!

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:15.840
You too.

00:15:00.690 --> 00:15:02.050
Ronja.

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:05.080
Comfort me.

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:08.700
Please help me through my grief.

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:21.500
Soon it will be spring again.

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:25.250
You'll feel better then.

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:32.280
Skalle-Per won't see spring...

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:42.350
But winter passed and springtime came,

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:51.440
as it always did, whoever lived or whoever died.

00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:58.050
Let's go!

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:05.270
Mattis began to cheer up...

00:16:06.050 --> 00:16:10.330
As he did every spring.

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:26.330
I'm glad you never wanted to be a robber, Birk.

00:16:29.490 --> 00:16:32.580
Yeah, I took an oath, right?

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:39.100
But I do wonder what we're going to live on, you and I.

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:44.330
I know how we'll get by.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:51.250
When I was young, I spent my time
 in the woods, just like you.

00:16:57.990 --> 00:17:04.960
One day, I happened to save a little gray dwarf from some wild harpies.

00:17:06.320 --> 00:17:10.980
He was so grateful afterwards that I could scarcely get rid of him.

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:17.880
He guided me to a cave overflowing with silver nuggets.

00:17:20.130 --> 00:17:24.830
My little pride and joy.

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:31.000
When the time has come, you find that place.

00:17:31.490 --> 00:17:34.700
Yeah, I'll find it for sure.

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:42.240
And who knows? Maybe it's not just a fairy tale.

00:17:42.610 --> 00:17:47.010
Skalle-Per swore it was true.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:52.680
We can ride up there and have a look someday.

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:56.500
I know where it is.

00:17:57.850 --> 00:18:01.480
But it's not a thing we have to do in hurry at all.

00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:10.410
Just make sure you keep it secret.

00:18:10.410 --> 00:18:11.520
Otherwise...

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:19.510
All the robbers will be in a rush to snatch up all that silver.

00:18:24.930 --> 00:18:28.040
You're as wise as Skalle-Per.

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:32.940
That's why I couldn't tell anyone but you.

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:39.470
But for the time being, we'll be alright without silver.

00:18:39.890 --> 00:18:42.430
Isn't that right? My sister.

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:43.980
Yup.

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:50.200
In the Bear's Cave, we need more important things.

00:18:53.490 --> 00:19:01.840
But, what will Mattis say if he hears we're going to move there again soon?

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:09.750
Oh, Ronja hasn't come back yet.

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:13.260
No, I came here to see you.

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:21.760
My old cave, huh?

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:25.470
Yeah, that's wonderful.

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:30.360
There's no better place to live at this time of year.

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:39.750
Don't you think so, Lovis?

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:42.800
You can go, Ronja.

00:19:43.300 --> 00:19:45.950
If your father says so.

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:52.740
But I'll be lonely without you.

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:03.970
However!

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:09.770
You <i>will</i> come home in the fall, right?

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:12.080
Like you usually do.

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:19.420
Yes, I'll do what I always do.

00:20:19.420 --> 00:20:20.170
Right?

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:20.690
Yup.

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:24.720
And that cave is really mine.

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:26.740
Don't you forget it.

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:31.880
So I might come and visit you from time to time.

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:35.290
I'm fine with that.

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:45.760
But it'll be a relief not having to see that curly, black-haired mug of yours every day.

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:49.700
Yeah, you're absolutely right!

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.320
I'm off now!

00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:30.160
I'm leaving, Mom!

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:34.390
Take care.

00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:06.630
Pelje!

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:07.890
Hey!

